WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:16.460
*intro music* dooo doo doooo

00:00:16.460 --> 00:00:19.480
Hello Internet! Welcome to Film Theory!

00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:24.000
Where I can't waste anymore time getting to the finale of this theory,

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:29.420
because I keep literally being stopped in the streets and asked what one is the deadliest movie is gonna end up being.

00:00:29.420 --> 00:00:33.600
It's actually a little unsettling how into this theory everyone is.

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:38.820
Plus, the process of getting through these last 5 EXCRUCIATINGLY historically inaccurate movies

00:00:38.820 --> 00:00:42.860
is going to take us so long that I literally don't have any time to waste today.

00:00:42.860 --> 00:00:45.480
No witty banter, no cringey dad jokes, :((((((

00:00:45.480 --> 00:00:48.900
Just death, death, and even more DEATH-ok.....-

00:00:48.960 --> 00:00:54.960
Remember, we ended last episode with our total kill count sitting at three thousand, five hundred and twenty.

00:00:54.960 --> 00:00:57.280
(I forgot to add a two at the end of last episode)

00:00:57.320 --> 00:01:01.920
Those three thousand, five hundred twenty deaths were comin' across fifty three movies.

00:01:02.060 --> 00:01:06.340
The top of our deadliest Disney movie leaderboard belonged to "The Lion King", (survival of the fittest am i right?)

00:01:06.500 --> 00:01:12.540
sitting confidently atop pride rock and a pile o' bones with one thousand, six hundred and sixty lives lost, (oh snap!)

00:01:12.700 --> 00:01:15.860
mostly due to a half a decade of hyenas overfeeding.

00:01:15.860 --> 00:01:21.080
But get ready because today's challengers are gonna give that number a heck of a run for its money.

00:01:21.080 --> 00:01:22.628
When we started in on this trilogy,

00:01:22.628 --> 00:01:27.140
everyone on our Theorist Team picked the movie that
they thought was gonna end up being the deadliest.

00:01:27.140 --> 00:01:29.420
It's like guessing the weight
of a new baby before it's born,

00:01:29.420 --> 00:01:33.600
except instead of pounds and ounces, it's
beheadings and extinction-level events! (I wonder what system this measurement this is!)

00:01:33.610 --> 00:01:38.180
Hopefully, your pick made it as a
finalist because this is your last chance to get those bets in!

00:01:38.180 --> 00:01:39.900
Your final five, Internet:

00:01:39.900 --> 00:01:44.360
Mulan, Dinosaur, Hercules, Atlantis or Moana! (Mulan is by far the deadliest in my eyes)

00:01:44.360 --> 00:01:46.940
Or heck,  maybe it's just gonna stay "The Lion King". (maybe!)

00:01:46.940 --> 00:01:47.780
Choose wisely,

00:01:47.780 --> 00:01:52.400
because
lives, and more importantly, internet bragging rights, depend on it.

00:01:52.400 --> 00:01:56.640
Let's start
with what is bizarrely the most straightforward of these final five:

00:01:56.640 --> 00:01:57.480
Mulan

00:01:57.480 --> 00:02:00.520
which was a clear fan favorite for death count in the comments.

00:02:00.520 --> 00:02:01.700
And I understand why.

00:02:01.700 --> 00:02:04.440
I mean, you literally see two villages burned,

00:02:04.440 --> 00:02:07.980
an army of good guys
just outright dead in the snow,

00:02:07.980 --> 00:02:09.820
and the climax of the whole thing is,

00:02:09.820 --> 00:02:10.800
as we all remember,

00:02:10.800 --> 00:02:13.360
Mulan using fireworks to cause an avalanche,

00:02:13.360 --> 00:02:16.560
that buries all but six of
the invading Hun army. (ThaT's alOt of dAmaGe!)

00:02:16.560 --> 00:02:20.530
Initially, I thought the best way to do this would be
to just look at history. (History saves da day!)

00:02:20.530 --> 00:02:23.140
Mulan the Disney movie, in case you
didn't know,

00:02:23.140 --> 00:02:25.340
comes from the Chinese legend of Hua Mulan,

00:02:25.340 --> 00:02:29.540
where the female
warrior, Mulan, does what the movie would teach us to expect her to do,

00:02:29.540 --> 00:02:33.140
she takes
her aging father's place in the army to defend against invaders.

00:02:33.140 --> 00:02:36.640
Interestingly enough, though, this is a really progressive story.

00:02:36.640 --> 00:02:39.629
In the original
legend, she doesn't hide her true self

00:02:39.629 --> 00:02:42.400
from her family, or sneak away in the
middle of the night.

00:02:42.400 --> 00:02:46.540
Her family totally supports her decision to become a
kick-butt warrior woman. (who wouldn't?)

00:02:46.540 --> 00:02:49.240
And she doesn't even need to fall in love with another soldier.

00:02:49.240 --> 00:02:53.240
I mean, I get that Disney needed to create some conflict or something,

00:02:53.240 --> 00:02:58.860
but the 5th century historical version of this story is actually a lot cooler, (cooler than that avalanche?)

00:02:58.860 --> 00:03:03.140
and
a lot more progressive than the 1998 remake.

00:03:03.140 --> 00:03:04.340
Feels bad man. D': (KERMIT NOOOOOOOO)

00:03:04.340 --> 00:03:07.840
Given that it's a
legend, maaaaaaaybe based in some history,

00:03:07.840 --> 00:03:12.260
I thought we could estimate deaths based
on the number of soldiers in Shan Yu's real army. (He was real?!!)

00:03:12.260 --> 00:03:16.240
Buuuuuuuut Shan Yu isn't a real person. (Oh ok! Almost had a brain-splosion there)

00:03:16.240 --> 00:03:20.080
If anyone, he's sort of super loosely based on Attila the Hun,

00:03:20.080 --> 00:03:25.320
but geographically, Attila's Empire ended 3,000 miles west of the Northern Wei
Empire,

00:03:25.320 --> 00:03:26.840
where the Mulan legend originates.

00:03:26.840 --> 00:03:30.180
And most of his battles were fought
against Europeans.

00:03:30.180 --> 00:03:31.840
So we got ourselves the wrong enemy,

00:03:31.840 --> 00:03:33.560
at the wrong end of the continent.

00:03:33.560 --> 00:03:36.440
So there were really no Attila battles that I could base this on.

00:03:36.440 --> 00:03:37.940
But, I kept on trying (You always do!)

00:03:37.940 --> 00:03:42.160
Shan Yu gets his name from the anglicized version of Chanyu title,

00:03:42.160 --> 00:03:44.700
which is just the generic term for a Hun leader.

00:03:44.700 --> 00:03:47.840
It would be like watching a
movie about America a thousand years from now,

00:03:47.840 --> 00:03:51.180
where the head of our country
was somehow named Perez O'Dent!

00:03:51.180 --> 00:03:53.800
Given that Chanyu is this totally generic title,

00:03:53.800 --> 00:03:57.600
there is still no battle that we could possibly base this finale of Mulan on.

00:03:57.600 --> 00:04:01.780
It also doesn't help us that there's no real historical record of Mulan. (whAaaAaAaAaAaAaaAaT?)

00:04:01.780 --> 00:04:06.187
While her legend is really famous, she's usually left out of Chinese history texts (probs cause she was a woman)

00:04:06.187 --> 00:04:10.220
and seems to be treated like a symbol rather than a real historical person.(ok nevermind)

00:04:10.220 --> 00:04:12.900
So in the end, with not enough credible information to go on,

00:04:12.900 --> 00:04:17.160
I had to result to doing a death count the old-fashioned way: counting.

00:04:17.160 --> 00:04:18.690
Except that counting all these people

00:04:18.690 --> 00:04:21.740
the old-fashioned way would have taken a
ridiculous amount of time,

00:04:21.740 --> 00:04:24.860
so I did it the new fashioned way: a Macro.

00:04:24.860 --> 00:04:26.280
Using
GNU Octave,

00:04:26.280 --> 00:04:31.360
I processed the frames of Mulan to automatically count how large Shan Yu's horde was.

00:04:31.360 --> 00:04:34.040
The program converts the images into black and white,

00:04:34.040 --> 00:04:38.300
which, in turn, makes it easier for the computer to count the individual members of the army.

00:04:38.300 --> 00:04:40.720
I had to really fiddle around with the settings here,

00:04:40.720 --> 00:04:43.740
to make sure that the program only was counting what I wanted it to,

00:04:43.740 --> 00:04:45.340
soon to be dead Huns.

00:04:45.340 --> 00:04:46.920
After some creative photoshopping,

00:04:46.920 --> 00:04:51.020
I came out with eleven deaths on the
mountainside by aggressive firework,

00:04:51.020 --> 00:04:53.920
plus an additional hundred and seventy-eight horsemen,

00:04:53.920 --> 00:04:58.540
and one thousand and forty-eight other soldiers in the avalanche itself, (oh snap!)

00:04:58.540 --> 00:05:03.560
for a grand total of one thousand, two hundred and thirty-seven kills.

00:05:03.560 --> 00:05:05.820
Add to that the two villages that we see burned,

00:05:05.820 --> 00:05:08.840
which, based on the size and proximity to the Great Wall of China,

00:05:08.840 --> 00:05:10.920
would have had about a hundred residents each.

00:05:10.920 --> 00:05:14.820
As well as the army that gets
massacred trying to surprise attack Shan Yu,

00:05:14.820 --> 00:05:17.680
which we can count in these scenes
to be thirty-one,

00:05:17.680 --> 00:05:19.780
but actually only adds thirty deaths,

00:05:19.780 --> 00:05:21.760
since one messenger survives the
massacre.

00:05:21.760 --> 00:05:24.200
"How many men does it take to deliver a message?"

00:05:24.200 --> 00:05:25.660
*Awkward silence*

00:05:25.660 --> 00:05:26.520
"One..."

00:05:26.520 --> 00:05:27.960
And then Shan Yu
himself,

00:05:27.960 --> 00:05:33.160
we get ourselves a grand total of one thousand, four hundred and sixty-eight.

00:05:33.160 --> 00:05:38.300
It's worth noting here that I've
seen a few other different versions of this death count circulating around online,

00:05:38.300 --> 00:05:41.180
ranging anywhere from two hundred and sixty,

00:05:41.180 --> 00:05:43.500
to the upwards of two thousand.

00:05:43.500 --> 00:05:46.780
I was
as absolutely exhaustive in this analysis as possible,

00:05:46.780 --> 00:05:50.026
so I feel pretty darn good about that one thousand four-hundred and sixty-eight number,

00:05:50.026 --> 00:05:53.700
but in the end, it still doesn't edge out The Lion King.

00:05:53.700 --> 00:05:54.820
With
Mulan out of the way, (Nuuuuuu)

00:05:54.820 --> 00:05:58.640
it's time to move on to the last of our movies in the princess category.

00:05:58.640 --> 00:06:03.680
Going from Mulan in China-ish to Moana in Polynesia-ish.

00:06:03.680 --> 00:06:06.540
After this, it's all gods and natural disasters,

00:06:06.540 --> 00:06:10.720
so Moana is gonna be our last hope for a princess to take home the murder crown.

00:06:10.720 --> 00:06:13.539
Grandma Tala becomes
death number one early on in the movie,

00:06:13.540 --> 00:06:17.880
and death number two quickly skyrockets
to death number two hundred and sixty,

00:06:17.880 --> 00:06:22.060
when Maui and Moana blow up and sink an entire society of Kakamora,

00:06:22.060 --> 00:06:23.600
the little coconut pirates they meet,

00:06:23.600 --> 00:06:27.426
in that totally forgettable scene that's just sandwiched in the middle of the movie.

00:06:27.426 --> 00:06:31.420
Anyway, those little
scamps are based on a Solomon Islands legend of the Kakamora,

00:06:31.420 --> 00:06:34.780
a race of very small people who would steal from island tribes.

00:06:34.780 --> 00:06:37.580
They're always
depicted as cute and harmless.

00:06:37.580 --> 00:06:42.420
Which is clearly why Moana and Maui feel it necessary to sink two hundred and fifty-nine of them,

00:06:42.420 --> 00:06:45.160
at my best count, mercilessly into the ocean,

00:06:45.160 --> 00:06:47.680
and then smile about it to each other as they sail away,

00:06:47.680 --> 00:06:50.220
leaving no survivors in their wake.

00:06:50.220 --> 00:06:51.340
"We did it!"

00:06:51.340 --> 00:06:52.320
Ba-rutal!

00:06:52.320 --> 00:06:54.000
Okay, that's two hundred and sixty.

00:06:54.000 --> 00:06:57.400
It's certainly a bloodbath, but it is far from record-breaking,

00:06:57.400 --> 00:06:59.560
but now we get to the curse.

00:06:59.560 --> 00:07:04.800
The whole movie hinges on the fact that Maui stole this powerful heart of Te Fiti,

00:07:04.800 --> 00:07:07.880
and thereby brought about a thousand-year plague.

00:07:07.880 --> 00:07:14.000
"Without her heart,
Te Fiti began to crumble, giving birth to a terrible darkness, (Darkrai is that you?)

00:07:14.100 --> 00:07:21.980
that will continue to spread until every one of us is devoured by inescapable death!"

00:07:21.980 --> 00:07:27.880
That means that Maui would be
responsible for a thousand years of darkness spreading across the Pacific Islands,

00:07:27.880 --> 00:07:31.280
which seems like it should be a shoo-in for death and destruction.

00:07:31.280 --> 00:07:33.400
I am certainly excited. &gt;:D

00:07:33.400 --> 00:07:37.040
Now we do have to remember that except for a single crab god,

00:07:37.040 --> 00:07:39.640
animal species aren't sapient in this movie.

00:07:39.640 --> 00:07:41.380
So fish aren't gonna count.

00:07:41.380 --> 00:07:44.480
And as much as I'd like to think that that leaves us with plenty of room for death,

00:07:44.480 --> 00:07:50.270
the problem with this curse quickly becomes the fact that it's just now showing up to Moana's island

00:07:50.270 --> 00:07:54.439
which means that it has been coming for
a looooooong time.

00:07:54.439 --> 00:07:58.740
Sure, Grandma's map at the beginning of
the movie shows this darkness spreading really fast,

00:07:58.740 --> 00:08:01.500
and yet when Moana and her dad visit the top of the island,

00:08:01.500 --> 00:08:05.360
he shows her how long they've been living there without any issues.

00:08:05.360 --> 00:08:09.300
No darkness to contend with, for
at my count, twelve generations.

00:08:09.300 --> 00:08:13.819
If we're being generous and say that a generation of leader is turning over every 25 years,

00:08:13.819 --> 00:08:17.509
which again, Moana's dad looks
significantly older than this but we're

00:08:17.509 --> 00:08:19.160
giving it a worst-case scenario,

00:08:19.160 --> 00:08:26.820
we're looking at at least 300 years of easy fish and coconuts, without even a hint of a plague.

00:08:26.820 --> 00:08:29.860
I mean if you have that long to become a doomsday prepper,

00:08:29.860 --> 00:08:32.300
and you don't build in any contingency plans,

00:08:32.300 --> 00:08:34.660
I think there's an argument to be made that you might have had it coming. (corona virus anyone?)

00:08:34.660 --> 00:08:39.940
Anyway the point is, we need to see if this darkness is actually creeping up on anyone,

00:08:39.940 --> 00:08:42.460
or if it's just totally avoidable.

00:08:42.460 --> 00:08:45.400
To figure that out, we're gonna have to measure how far the curse has traveled.

00:08:45.400 --> 00:08:47.630
Which, we know
is gonna be from the heart of Te Fiti,

00:08:47.630 --> 00:08:51.220
where the curse started, to Moana's
Island at the start of the movie.

00:08:51.220 --> 00:08:55.600
So all we need to know is how far she travels in her boat between those two locations

00:08:55.600 --> 00:08:57.300
and how long it takes to get there.

00:08:57.300 --> 00:09:01.722
Here's what we know, we see Moana travel for three, maybe four days at most,

00:09:01.722 --> 00:09:03.740
her boat is captained by Maui,

00:09:03.740 --> 00:09:05.460
a master wayfinder and demigod,

00:09:05.460 --> 00:09:08.060
and her boat is a recreation of a Fijian camakau, (say: camikaw)

00:09:08.060 --> 00:09:09.920
similar to an out-rigger canoe,

00:09:09.920 --> 00:09:11.780
that can travel up to 15 knots,

00:09:11.780 --> 00:09:14.260
or, 17 MPH.

00:09:14.260 --> 00:09:16.480
We're gonna somehow have
to ignore the fact

00:09:16.480 --> 00:09:22.080
that this boat was also built by those three hundred year old ancestors who landed on Moana's Island,

00:09:22.080 --> 00:09:25.980
making this boat so impossibly
old that there's no way it would actually sail,

00:09:25.980 --> 00:09:27.500
but, whatever Disney.

00:09:27.500 --> 00:09:31.160
We'll also assume that Moana didn't sleep at any point during the journey,

00:09:31.160 --> 00:09:34.380
something Maui considered a sign of weakness as a wayfinder. (gosh she looks bad)

00:09:34.380 --> 00:09:36.120
So at the boats max rate,

00:09:36.120 --> 00:09:39.120
steered completely straight by an expert wayfinder,

00:09:39.120 --> 00:09:42.440
she could sail one thousand six-hundred and thirty-two miles,

00:09:42.440 --> 00:09:45.860
or two thousand six-hundred and twenty-six kilometers, in four days,

00:09:45.860 --> 00:09:50.029
which is pretty incredible but we're
giving them the best-case scenario.

00:09:50.029 --> 00:09:56.780
This means that Moana's island is a
little over sixteen-hundred miles from the heart of Te Fiti, or curse ground zero.

00:09:56.780 --> 00:09:59.240
So okay, if the darkness started at Te Fiti,

00:09:59.240 --> 00:10:02.880
and is just now reaching Moana's Island at least three-hundred years later,

00:10:02.880 --> 00:10:08.150
we're saying that it took three-hundred years for the darkness to spread sixteen hundred and thirty-two miles.

00:10:08.150 --> 00:10:13.600
Meaning that the curse has spread 5.4
miles per year.

00:10:13.600 --> 00:10:15.200
That is NOTHING!!

00:10:15.200 --> 00:10:16.820
When you're standing on the shore of a beach,

00:10:16.820 --> 00:10:20.100
the horizon you're seeing is 2.8 miles away.

00:10:20.100 --> 00:10:25.220
From the top of Moana's Island,
you would be seeing well over 12 miles into the horizon.

00:10:25.220 --> 00:10:31.100
You would literally see
this darkness coming towards your shores for several years in advance,

00:10:31.100 --> 00:10:34.040
which is why Moana's deadliness just falls apart.

00:10:34.040 --> 00:10:35.280
With that much notice,

00:10:35.280 --> 00:10:39.820
it would be almost impossible to believe that seafaring Polynesian island dwellers,

00:10:39.820 --> 00:10:41.860
who primarily fish for survival,

00:10:41.860 --> 00:10:46.960
would be unable to, you know, get in their boats and sail to the next island over when they see the curse coming,

00:10:46.960 --> 00:10:49.260
thereby buying them a few extra years.

00:10:49.260 --> 00:10:55.240
Even Moana's tribe of people who are water-phobic are still gonna have time to see their shriveled coconuts,

00:10:55.240 --> 00:10:58.160
throw some Flex Tape onto those centuries-old boats,

00:10:58.160 --> 00:11:01.320
and move to the next island, which would buy them more time.

00:11:01.320 --> 00:11:06.380
So the final death tally for Moana, two hundred and sixty-one.(OMG SO LOW)

00:11:06.380 --> 00:11:08.580
Not. even. close.

00:11:08.580 --> 00:11:11.560
After a thoroughly disappointing performance by Moana,

00:11:11.560 --> 00:11:14.800
it's up to the last three movies to knock my socks off,

00:11:14.800 --> 00:11:16.977
and I'm confident in the next two:

00:11:16.977 --> 00:11:19.960
Atlantis: The Lost Empire and Hercules.

00:11:19.960 --> 00:11:25.820
Sure, Atlantis: The Lost Empire ain't one of those beloved Disney classics, with a big plastic VHS cover,

00:11:25.820 --> 00:11:28.560
but looking back on it, it's pretty darn good,

00:11:28.560 --> 00:11:31.100
and at the very
least, it is pretty darn deadly.

00:11:31.100 --> 00:11:32.900
But at this point, that's all I really care about.

00:11:32.900 --> 00:11:34.520
And since "We're in the endgame now",

00:11:34.520 --> 00:11:37.860
it's gonna need to prove itself in gladiatorial fashion,

00:11:37.860 --> 00:11:40.960
against another strong challenger from the same part of the world, Hercules!

00:11:40.960 --> 00:11:45.440
In one corner we've got ourself a flood that wrecks an entire civilization,

00:11:45.440 --> 00:11:49.940
and in the other we have ourselves a complete war between gods and Titans,

00:11:49.940 --> 00:11:52.580
with the world of man caught stuck in the middle.

00:11:52.580 --> 00:11:56.100
So let's set up those dueling
death tickers and get down to it.

00:11:56.100 --> 00:11:59.900
"Atlantis" there's a big chase scene with
a Leviathan early on in the movie,

00:11:59.900 --> 00:12:04.340
that accounts for one-hundred and seventy-one deaths right off the bat. (OUCH...)

00:12:04.340 --> 00:12:09.560
Adding in the King's death, and the ending battle, we suddenly jump up to a hundred and eighty-five.

00:12:09.560 --> 00:12:13.580
Though it can be hard to tell how many of the explosions we see signifying certain death,

00:12:13.580 --> 00:12:14.820
and how many
are just like,

00:12:14.820 --> 00:12:17.080
"Pew pew pew! Boom boom! Bhlur bhlur!"

00:12:17.080 --> 00:12:20.080
As I believe is the technical term of what we're watching. (i thought you said no banter.)

00:12:20.080 --> 00:12:23.935
Hercules His kills are mostly taking place during the montage

00:12:23.940 --> 00:12:27.200
of him completing some of the most famous twelve labors of Hercules.

00:12:27.200 --> 00:12:30.920
Herc' kills the Hydra, Erymanthian boar,  the Nemean Lion which

00:12:30.930 --> 00:12:32.685
(looks suspiciously like Scar),

00:12:32.685 --> 00:12:35.120
a sea monster that isn't part of the labors,

00:12:35.130 --> 00:12:36.740
but we'll give him credit for anyway,

00:12:36.740 --> 00:12:39.940
and then the Minotaur, a Gorgon and some really scary looking bird.

00:12:39.940 --> 00:12:44.660
Two of which were actually fought by the Greek hero Perseus, but you get the idea.

00:12:44.660 --> 00:12:48.740
We can also give Hercules credit for killing Nessus, the Centaur that's torturing Meg.

00:12:48.740 --> 00:12:52.920
It's unclear in the movie if he's officially dead or if he's just unconscious,

00:12:52.920 --> 00:12:57.810
but according to Greek myth Hercules does indeed kill him, so we're gonna go with that.

00:12:57.810 --> 00:12:59.660
and no, we're not counting Meg,

00:12:59.660 --> 00:13:03.040
sure, she dies, but she has to die and stay dead.

00:13:03.040 --> 00:13:04.660
Meg gets revived before the end of
the movie.

00:13:04.660 --> 00:13:08.120
Also, you can't count Hades, because he already lives in the underworld.

00:13:08.120 --> 00:13:10.360
So, based off of these early action sequences,

00:13:10.360 --> 00:13:14.040
Atlantis: The Lost Empire has a significant lead,

00:13:14.040 --> 00:13:16.840
but at the end of the day, this isn't really gonna matter.

00:13:16.840 --> 00:13:23.500
Because these numbers are tiny, compared
to the huge catastrophic events in both movies.

00:13:23.500 --> 00:13:25.980
The sinking of Atlantis, and the
Titanomachy.

00:13:25.980 --> 00:13:28.480
And here's where the counting has to get creative.

00:13:28.480 --> 00:13:34.620
Atlantis: The Lost Empire starts with a giant tsunami headed for the island of Atlantis.

00:13:34.620 --> 00:13:38.520
A protective barrier, bubble, thing is formed around the center of the island,

00:13:38.520 --> 00:13:40.320
and sinks into the ocean.

00:13:40.320 --> 00:13:43.200
It's not as though everyone in Atlantis dies,

00:13:43.200 --> 00:13:46.880
but we do see a lot of people banging on that bubble from the outside,

00:13:46.880 --> 00:13:52.480
and the bubble only ends up saving just a small fraction of the land of Atlantis.(ouch...)

00:13:52.480 --> 00:13:56.220
Which leaves us with an obvious question, and the not so obvious answer:

00:13:56.220 --> 00:13:59.400
How many people die when Atlantis sinks?

00:13:59.480 --> 00:14:04.980
It'd be nearly impossible to get a decent guess at this just from the design of the city that we see at the beginning of the movie,

00:14:04.980 --> 00:14:10.650
so we're gonna have to go all the way back to the ancient Greek Atlantis story to determine the most likely death toll.

00:14:10.650 --> 00:14:14.280
Ditto for when Hades releases the
Titans onto Earth and they start wrecking house.

00:14:14.280 --> 00:14:15.880
Let's start with Atlantis.

00:14:15.880 --> 00:14:21.360
From a historical perspective, all our information about Atlantis comes from the Greek philosopher Plato.

00:14:21.360 --> 00:14:25.820
You know, the Plato who tells a story about a farmer who finds himself a ring

00:14:25.820 --> 00:14:28.780
that makes him invisible but corrupts him morally.

00:14:28.780 --> 00:14:32.260
A story that J.R.R Tolkien deeeefinitely didn't steal.

00:14:32.260 --> 00:14:37.100
Anyway, in his dialogue
"Critias", Plato tells of the continent Atlantis,

00:14:37.100 --> 00:14:42.420
a 10,000 BC superpower with a
great military and tons of technology,

00:14:42.420 --> 00:14:49.280
so advanced that it sank because the gods
got jealous and sent a big earthquake/flood combo to take it down. (it's super effective!)

00:14:49.280 --> 00:14:54.800
Sounds fine, cool myth bro, but Plato never mentions how many people live on
Atlantis,

00:14:54.800 --> 00:14:57.800
which would have really done a lot to make my life easier.

00:14:57.800 --> 00:15:07.270
Bizarrely, the mythical estimates for Atlantis's army ranges from 5 million to over 100 million, and everything in between.

00:15:07.270 --> 00:15:10.180
but regardless, those numbers give us a
bit of an issue,

00:15:10.180 --> 00:15:14.706
because the population of the entire world at the time in
10,000 BC,

00:15:14.706 --> 00:15:19.220
would have been somewhere in the order of 1 to 3 million people!

00:15:19.220 --> 00:15:23.115
Adding insult to injury, Atlantis probably isn't even from
10,000 BC,

00:15:23.120 --> 00:15:28.220
because a mistranslation basically changed the entire story to nine thousand years ago,

00:15:28.220 --> 00:15:31.260
when it was originally meant to be nine hundred
years ago.

00:15:31.260 --> 00:15:37.860
So basically, TL;DR, we're looking for some
historical event that Plato could have based his clearly made-up story on,

00:15:37.860 --> 00:15:41.980
that he then used to pass off as if it were historically true to all his bros.

00:15:41.980 --> 00:15:45.640
So what historic clues can we find in Atlantis the movie?

00:15:45.640 --> 00:15:49.480
Well, the one thing we
actually know is that there was a tsunami.

00:15:49.480 --> 00:15:52.780
So we just have to find a
massive historical tsunami

00:15:52.780 --> 00:15:55.460
at the right time and place to make this happen,

00:15:55.460 --> 00:15:57.680
and for that ladies and gentlemen, I give you:

00:15:57.680 --> 00:15:59.460
The Minoan civilization.

00:15:59.460 --> 00:16:06.560
Located on the island of Crete and most prominent from about 2000 to 1500 BC.

00:16:06.560 --> 00:16:12.209
The Minoans are most famous for building palaces and being the inspiration for the myth of the Minotaur,

00:16:12.209 --> 00:16:16.540
but Minoans are also our best proxy for
both Atlantis as Plato reported it,

00:16:16.540 --> 00:16:19.500
as well as how Disney imagined it.

00:16:19.500 --> 00:16:22.860
The large buildings that we see present in Atlantis: the Lost Empire

00:16:22.860 --> 00:16:25.980
would have been extraordinarily rare in the ancient world,

00:16:25.980 --> 00:16:29.880
but the Minoans were building
palaces and multi-story buildings

00:16:29.880 --> 00:16:33.620
earlier than any other island
civilization that we know of.

00:16:33.620 --> 00:16:37.540
The Minoan language also checks off the boxes from what we see in the movie.

00:16:37.540 --> 00:16:40.280
Nobody is really sure what Minoan sounded like,

00:16:40.280 --> 00:16:44.700
because we can't read the basic Minoan writing system known as "Linear A",

00:16:44.700 --> 00:16:48.826
which parallels the fact that no one can read Atlantean in the movie itself.

00:16:48.826 --> 00:16:51.420
"Yes, yes, I can read Atlantean just like you."

00:16:51.420 --> 00:16:53.720
"You can't, can you?

00:16:53.720 --> 00:16:54.880
"No one can."

00:16:54.880 --> 00:17:00.400
And most importantly of all, we have an event that would make sense for the "sinking" of Atlantis.

00:17:00.400 --> 00:17:02.560
Around 1550 BC,

00:17:02.560 --> 00:17:07.680
right around the real time Atlantis was supposed to be set without Plato screwing up his dates,

00:17:07.680 --> 00:17:11.059
the volcanic island of Thera- modern-day Santorini,

00:17:11.059 --> 00:17:16.620
exploded, destroying part of the island
and sending gigantic waves to the shores of Crete,

00:17:16.620 --> 00:17:18.040
only about 70 miles away.

00:17:18.040 --> 00:17:21.200
The resulting tsunami devastated the coast of Crete,

00:17:21.200 --> 00:17:23.780
destroying cities, ruining coastline,

00:17:23.780 --> 00:17:26.400
and of course killing a lot of people.

00:17:26.400 --> 00:17:29.780
Now I hear ya, Atlantis is
supposed to have sunk into the sea,

00:17:29.780 --> 00:17:32.580
and Crete is still very much around.

00:17:32.580 --> 00:17:36.000
That said, part of the island of Thera sank,

00:17:36.000 --> 00:17:39.740
you can actually see where a bunch of it
is missing even to this day.

00:17:39.740 --> 00:17:45.560
So the whole idea is still right, for this event sunk an island and destroyed a civilization.

00:17:45.560 --> 00:17:49.920
So for God's sake, after all of that over
analysis, what the heck is the death count?

00:17:49.920 --> 00:17:55.400
Well, estimates have the eruption
of Thera killing 35,000 Minoans on Crete.

00:17:55.400 --> 00:17:59.160
Wow. That's to say nothing of the people
who are on Thera itself.

00:17:59.160 --> 00:18:01.620
Even if we want to use a more conservative estimate,

00:18:01.620 --> 00:18:05.920
those estimates still run in the range of twenty thousand deaths.

00:18:05.920 --> 00:18:10.620
Definitely enough to dwarf any of our other Disney contenders up to this point.

00:18:10.620 --> 00:18:14.400
So as devastating a historical event as this was based on,

00:18:14.400 --> 00:18:20.200
the silver lining here is that in the Disney version there is no way "Hercules" can beat this, right?

00:18:20.200 --> 00:18:23.320
I mean, sure, houses are crushed, temples are blown away,

00:18:23.320 --> 00:18:27.040
but it can't measure up to the explosion of Thera, right?

00:18:27.040 --> 00:18:33.720
Except, interestingly enough, many people believe that the inspiration for the story of the Titanomachy,

00:18:33.720 --> 00:18:39.820
the exact scenes that we see take place in Hercules, was the massive eruption of Thera.

00:18:39.820 --> 00:18:42.940
The same event that we just attributed to the loss of Atlantis.

00:18:42.940 --> 00:18:49.000
So the long story short here is
that the destruction in these two movies are based on the exact same event.

00:18:49.000 --> 00:18:51.000
So what is it, like a tie, then?

00:18:51.000 --> 00:18:52.480
I mean, effectively.

00:18:52.480 --> 00:18:57.280
For as much as we can calculate real numbers out of poorly documented historical facts,

00:18:57.280 --> 00:19:01.020
that influenced fictional movies hundreds of years later, yeah.

00:19:01.020 --> 00:19:05.600
Although Hercules is taking place in Thebes, which is much farther away from Thera than Crete is,

00:19:05.600 --> 00:19:09.980
so there would be fewer deaths associated with Hercules just by proximity alone.

00:19:09.980 --> 00:19:13.380
There you have it. Hercules and Atlantis practically in a tie.

00:19:13.380 --> 00:19:16.740
I mean, of the two, Atlantis would qualify as the more deadly movie,

00:19:16.740 --> 00:19:19.980
with Hercules in second
place, but the two of them have a commanding lead

00:19:19.980 --> 00:19:23.580
over anything else in the Disney canon that we've covered so far.

00:19:23.580 --> 00:19:28.560
Congratulations, Disney, on leveraging a devastating global event for children's entertainment,

00:19:28.560 --> 00:19:30.620
not just once but twice.

00:19:30.620 --> 00:19:32.000
But don't worry, I hear ya.

00:19:32.000 --> 00:19:33.720
"A tie? What?!"

00:19:33.720 --> 00:19:36.660
"You can't lead us through an entire flippin' trilogy on Disney movies,

00:19:36.660 --> 00:19:40.080
and ruin Christmas, and string us along through this ungodly long episode,

00:19:40.080 --> 00:19:44.200
that has itself a flippin' mid-roll just to tell us that it ends in a tie!"

00:19:44.200 --> 00:19:47.880
I mean, I don't write the movies, so take it up with old Walt.

00:19:47.880 --> 00:19:49.820
Oh wait! There is still one more.

00:19:49.820 --> 00:19:51.620
Dinosaur.

00:19:51.620 --> 00:19:52.640
That's right.

00:19:52.640 --> 00:19:56.880
The Disney feature you didn't know you needed and then definitely continue to not need,

00:19:56.880 --> 00:19:58.340
because it came out in 2000,

00:19:58.340 --> 00:20:02.760
and we already had the far superior Land Before Time series since 1988.

00:20:02.760 --> 00:20:06.030
But regardless, it's a movie
that the Disney Animation Studios made,

00:20:06.030 --> 00:20:10.960
and it is here where the buck stops when
it comes to Disney deaths.

00:20:10.960 --> 00:20:12.220
And I know you're all like

00:20:12.220 --> 00:20:17.380
"Oh! Of course! This movie shows the extinction, right? So many millions of dinosaurs died!",

00:20:17.380 --> 00:20:22.800
And as much as I'd like to just finally, finally end this with the mass extinction of the dinosaurs,

00:20:22.800 --> 00:20:25.920
this movie actually doesn't show that event.

00:20:25.920 --> 00:20:28.380
I swear, that would have
put the easy way out!

00:20:28.380 --> 00:20:31.800
But in the entire film, only five dinosaurs died.

00:20:31.800 --> 00:20:35.440
Two bad guys, two good guys and one neutral Triceratops.

00:20:35.440 --> 00:20:35.940
That's it.

00:20:35.940 --> 00:20:37.400
I know, I couldn't
believe it either!

00:20:37.410 --> 00:20:40.600
But if that's the case, then where else
could all the deaths come from?

00:20:40.600 --> 00:20:42.080
And the grand answer,

00:20:42.080 --> 00:20:48.424
the answer to where the most Disney deaths come from in the animation studio's 80-year history isn't coming from humans,

00:20:48.424 --> 00:20:50.240
isn't coming from fish,

00:20:50.240 --> 00:20:52.640
it's coming from lemurs.

00:20:52.640 --> 00:20:54.560
Yep. These guys.

00:20:54.560 --> 00:20:56.500
Prehistoric lemurs.

00:20:56.500 --> 00:20:58.640
You might be thinking to yourself,

00:20:58.640 --> 00:21:02.840
"Gee! I didn't think dinosaurs and lemurs really lived at the same time!"

00:21:02.840 --> 00:21:04.000
And right you would be!

00:21:04.000 --> 00:21:05.100
Pretty much.

00:21:05.100 --> 00:21:11.240
There's some research that mammals and dinosaurs did overlap for a very short time at the end of the Cretaceous period,

00:21:11.240 --> 00:21:14.820
when Aladar, our Iguanodon
protagonist, was supposed to have lived.

00:21:14.820 --> 00:21:18.620
And it just so happens that one of the
oldest animal species to exist

00:21:18.620 --> 00:21:23.380
in this teeny overlapping sweet spot 60 million years ago were lemurs.

00:21:23.380 --> 00:21:28.680
And yes, historically, you still have to really
squint at this one to get any kind of scenario

00:21:28.680 --> 00:21:30.860
where a monkey family would raise a dinosaur,

00:21:30.860 --> 00:21:33.820
but we're just gonna have to go with this one in order to make it to the other side of it.

00:21:33.820 --> 00:21:34.820
So, like I said,

00:21:34.820 --> 00:21:38.420
very few dinosaurs were actually harmed in the making of "Dinosaur",

00:21:38.420 --> 00:21:43.380
but an entire island worth of lemurs were just knocked out in one fell swoop.

00:21:43.380 --> 00:21:49.280
We see a meteor and the associated fallout land on the uncreatively named Lemur Island in the movie,

00:21:49.280 --> 00:21:51.720
sending the entire island up in flames,

00:21:51.720 --> 00:21:53.680
except for this small lemur family,

00:21:53.680 --> 00:21:55.480
and our friendly dinosaur hero.

00:21:55.480 --> 00:21:56.250
The lemur baby

00:21:56.250 --> 00:21:57.860
even comments that,

00:21:57.860 --> 00:22:00.060
"They're all...gone." :( (Geez that's dark)

00:22:00.060 --> 00:22:05.960
during the film, thereby confirming for us that every lemur on Lemur Island is now a crispy critter.

00:22:05.960 --> 00:22:09.060
But of course that leads to the next obvious question:

00:22:09.060 --> 00:22:14.560
How in the world do we know how many that is or even how big Lemur island is?

00:22:14.560 --> 00:22:17.140
Well, in the most
bizarre twist of luck,

00:22:17.140 --> 00:22:20.160
we actually know the real world location of Lemur Island,

00:22:20.160 --> 00:22:24.460
because historically there is only one possible location.

00:22:24.460 --> 00:22:28.190
It's the real island
off the East coast of Africa called...

00:22:28.190 --> 00:22:29.420
Madagascar.

00:22:29.420 --> 00:22:30.980
"I like to move it move it!"

00:22:30.980 --> 00:22:32.580
And your biology lesson for the day:

00:22:32.580 --> 00:22:38.740
The reason lemurs are lemurs is because they evolved all by themselves over millions of years,

00:22:38.740 --> 00:22:44.113
isolated from all other primate species on the lonely island of Madagascar.

00:22:44.120 --> 00:22:48.800
All lemurs, even modern lemurs, started back on Madagascar.

00:22:48.800 --> 00:22:54.023
So this is literally the only place Lemur Island could be in the entire planet Earth,

00:22:54.023 --> 00:22:57.060
especially on the order of 60 million years ago,

00:22:57.060 --> 00:23:00.300
when Madagascar had just started to separate from continental Africa.

00:23:00.300 --> 00:23:06.440
This is also why we only see the dinosaur and lemurs swimming across a narrow channel,

00:23:06.440 --> 00:23:08.240
rather than a huge body of water,

00:23:08.240 --> 00:23:10.060
in the aftermath of the meteor strike.

00:23:10.060 --> 00:23:16.020
At the time they escaped from Lemur Island, Lemur Island was just recently Lemur Peninsula.

00:23:16.020 --> 00:23:17.900
So with that incredible stroke of luck,

00:23:17.900 --> 00:23:22.070
we now know not only where Lemur
Island is, but how big it is.

00:23:22.070 --> 00:23:28.020
Madagascar is 226,597 square miles
in area.

00:23:28.020 --> 00:23:30.980
But not all of that area is habitable by lemurs.

00:23:30.980 --> 00:23:35.160
Going by its modern-day geography, which is honestly all we got,

00:23:35.160 --> 00:23:39.720
only about 43,000 square
miles of the island is rainforest,

00:23:39.720 --> 00:23:44.300
which is Lemur habitat and also the area where we see the lemurs living in the movies.

00:23:44.400 --> 00:23:50.720
So how many lemurs could reasonably be
living in 43,000 square miles of jungle?

00:23:50.800 --> 00:23:52.280
OOOOOOOOOOOOOHHHHHHHHHHHH!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!

00:23:52.280 --> 00:23:55.350
Well, this is impossible to know directly,

00:23:55.350 --> 00:24:00.020
but the lemurs in the movie would have
been precursors to the modern ring-tailed lemur,

00:24:00.020 --> 00:24:03.460
which has a territory size of 0.14 square miles.

00:24:03.460 --> 00:24:12.180
That means that you could fit yourself 307,143 lemurs on to Madagascar at territory capacity,

00:24:12.180 --> 00:24:15.940
which is how many lemurs we would have the potential to lose in Dinosaur.

00:24:15.940 --> 00:24:19.180
Even if we said it was half
that number,

00:24:19.180 --> 00:24:21.600
even if we said it was a tenth of that number,

00:24:21.600 --> 00:24:25.200
we still have our winner by
a long shot.

00:24:25.200 --> 00:24:32.520
By an apocalyptic landslide, Dinosaur is the deadliest Disney movie of all time.

00:24:32.520 --> 00:24:37.700
Rest in peace, lemurs, in a moment of
silence for all the Disney fallen who've gone before you.

00:24:37.760 --> 00:24:50.260
*CUE EMOTIONAL MUSIC*

00:24:50.260 --> 00:24:54.600
So after fifty-eight movies and three incredibly long episodes,

00:24:54.600 --> 00:24:56.880
what does all this mean, my friends?

00:24:56.880 --> 00:24:59.680
We have come a long way on the
Disney death train. (Or the d.d. train for short!)

00:24:59.683 --> 00:25:05.180
I wanted to highlight how much we've accomplished here by recapping some of our most significant findings.

00:25:05.180 --> 00:25:11.420
Across the entire Disney canon, fifty-eight original Disney animation studio movies,

00:25:11.420 --> 00:25:13.820
our estimated total deaths are...

00:25:13.820 --> 00:25:17.080
three-hundred and forty-four thousand and thirty one.

00:25:17.080 --> 00:25:22.820
Which is honestly nothing compared to the number of childhood dreams this show kills on a regular basis.

00:25:22.820 --> 00:25:24.480
(screaming child)

00:25:24.480 --> 00:25:31.729
Our overall deadliest Disney movie winner is "Dinosaur" and a death count of up to 300,000 sapient lemurs.

00:25:31.729 --> 00:25:34.560
The most deaths of any movie you cared about,

00:25:34.560 --> 00:25:36.340
or are likely to have seen
however,

00:25:36.340 --> 00:25:38.040
goes resoundingly to Hercules

00:25:38.040 --> 00:25:44.160
and Atlantis: The Lost Empire, with over
twenty to thirty thousand deaths each by volcano.

00:25:44.160 --> 00:25:46.320
Most deaths in a Disney princess movie,

00:25:46.320 --> 00:25:51.260
as well as Disney's deadliest princess goes to "Mulan" with just over twelve-hundred,

00:25:51.260 --> 00:25:52.740
very respectable number.

00:25:52.740 --> 00:25:56.540
Disney's deadliest and most effective villain is Scar, from "The Lion King",

00:25:56.540 --> 00:25:58.360
at sixteen-hundred and fifty-nine deaths.

00:25:58.360 --> 00:26:01.200
(The sixteen hundred and sixtieth death was his own.)

00:26:01.200 --> 00:26:03.800
Most twisted deaths go to "Alice in Wonderland",

00:26:03.800 --> 00:26:06.260
where the walrus eats twelve oyster babies.

00:26:06.260 --> 00:26:12.600
Most tragic death ends up going to the accidentally harpooned opera singing whale in "Make Mine Music".

00:26:12.600 --> 00:26:13.240
*sigh*

00:26:13.240 --> 00:26:14.680
Just brutally sad.

00:26:14.680 --> 00:26:20.920
And my personal favorite Disney death goes to Ursula being stabbed in the stomach at the end of "The Little Mermaid".

00:26:20.920 --> 00:26:25.700
And now, finally, with this series over and all this being said,

00:26:25.700 --> 00:26:33.420
you can now go and we can all collectively kill off 2018 to start the ol' kill count back at zero for 2019.

00:26:33.420 --> 00:26:39.700
This has been an incredibly fun but
totally exhausting project to finish off the year.

00:26:39.700 --> 00:26:42.620
I hope you enjoyed it as much
as I did. This was a blast.

00:26:42.620 --> 00:26:46.500
Let me know if you want me to do something similar for Pixar movies, Dreamworks movies,

00:26:46.500 --> 00:26:47.940
I don't know, I'm game for anything.

00:26:47.940 --> 00:26:50.460
Thank you so
much for your support over this three-part trilogy.

00:26:50.460 --> 00:26:53.070
Thank you so much for
your continued support of Film Theory,

00:26:53.070 --> 00:26:55.500
and have a Happy New Year everyone!

00:26:55.500 --> 00:26:57.680
Onward to 2019!

00:26:57.680 --> 00:27:00.020
I will see you there with more theories.

00:27:00.020 --> 00:27:02.040
More Film Theories!

00:27:02.540 --> 00:27:04.340
Aaaand cut.

